WEBVTT

00:03.650 --> 00:07.210
Your head will finally be mine today, Sunred!

00:07.210 --> 00:09.260
Demon Claw!

00:10.610 --> 00:11.340
He's so cute!

00:11.340 --> 00:13.380
Come on, get off me!

00:13.380 --> 00:16.160
You should be going home after school, not doing this!

00:16.160 --> 00:17.350
Dumbass.

00:17.350 --> 00:19.240
Don't you dare run away!

00:19.240 --> 00:21.130
You'll remember this, Red!

00:24.230 --> 00:26.330
In the city of Kawasaki, located in Kanagawa prefecture,

00:26.330 --> 00:28.570
exists a division of the evil organization known as Florsheim,

00:28.570 --> 00:31.590
whose main objective is to conquer the world.

00:31.590 --> 00:34.560
All of this looks so delicious!

00:35.160 --> 00:36.800
Try some of this, mister.

00:36.800 --> 00:37.920
Can I really?

00:37.920 --> 00:38.710
Of course you can.

00:39.380 --> 00:41.280
This is delicious!

00:41.280 --> 00:42.520
Thank you very much.

00:42.520 --> 00:44.440
You guys should try some of this too.

00:44.440 --> 00:44.830
Yes, sir.

00:46.340 --> 00:47.400
It really is delicious!

00:47.400 --> 00:48.600
The sea urchin's really good.

00:49.000 --> 00:51.070
I bet this would go really well with rice.

00:51.070 --> 00:53.200
The tarako slices are really firm.

00:53.200 --> 00:55.060
I love fried sweet potatoes.

00:55.060 --> 00:57.620
I bet some imojouchuu would top this off nicely.

00:57.620 --> 01:00.000
I can't make okonomiyaki like this at home.

01:00.000 --> 01:01.410
Nothing beats the original, I guess.

01:02.200 --> 01:04.830
I bet we'd be able to taste delicacies from all over Japan

01:04.830 --> 01:07.770
and even the whole world when we complete our world domination.

01:07.770 --> 01:09.350
Yeah.

01:09.350 --> 01:11.060
We better put our hearts into it.

01:11.060 --> 01:12.530
Thus inspired by the lure of delicacies,

01:12.530 --> 01:15.790
Florsheim renewed their ambition for world domination.

01:29.200 --> 01:30.830
That's so noisy!

01:31.660 --> 01:35.360
If that's noisy, when am I supposed to clean the house?

01:35.360 --> 01:37.490
Do you really have to do it now?

01:37.840 --> 01:39.330
Do I have a choice?

01:39.330 --> 01:41.030
I can only clean the house on my days off!

01:41.330 --> 01:43.820
It's all of a sudden noisy when you're not playing Pachinko, isn't it?

01:43.820 --> 01:44.730
If you really think I'm making that much noise,

01:44.730 --> 01:46.880
why don't you just go somewhere until I'm done cleaning!

03:19.850 --> 03:21.790
U-Um...

03:22.340 --> 03:23.450
Is that why you came to our house?

03:26.620 --> 03:28.160
I haven't had lunch yet.

03:28.160 --> 03:28.780
Give me something to eat.

03:28.780 --> 03:30.700
W-Wait a minute here.

03:30.820 --> 03:31.640
What's up.

03:32.240 --> 03:33.140
H-Hello.

03:33.140 --> 03:34.150
How are you?

03:34.750 --> 03:35.670
What's this?

03:36.910 --> 03:38.070
Um, well...

03:39.950 --> 03:41.910
Oh, my bad.

03:41.910 --> 03:43.240
I must be interrupting you guys.

03:43.240 --> 03:44.400
Oh I'm so sorry.

03:44.400 --> 03:45.690
You don't have to erase it!

03:49.190 --> 03:51.930
I'm sorry you had to make do with yesterday's seasoned rice.

03:51.930 --> 03:53.860
That stupid Kayoko...

03:53.860 --> 03:56.170
Did something happen to Kayoko?

03:56.170 --> 03:57.500
Nothing happened to her!

03:57.500 --> 03:59.520
Tell me if this sounds insensitive to you:

03:59.520 --> 04:03.320
She just started vacuuming and making all this noise out of nowhere, see?

04:03.320 --> 04:05.650
I wouldn't be complaining if she was actually good at cleaning,

04:05.980 --> 04:09.210
but this is basically all she does when she "cleans up."

04:09.450 --> 04:12.560
I mean it's easy for books to create a mess since they get all spread out or crumpled up

04:12.560 --> 04:15.890
like when you want a book at the bottom of the stack or if you need to move the pile to open the bottom drawer, right?

04:16.460 --> 04:21.330
Then she's been bitching at me since this morning about putting the toilet seat down,

04:21.330 --> 04:24.510
or making sure the free end of the saran wrap is not stuck and whatnot.

04:26.540 --> 04:27.910
What the hell?

04:27.910 --> 04:28.970
This guy's still here?

04:28.970 --> 04:29.860
Yeah.

04:30.140 --> 04:35.370
This is the mysterious creature that suddenly took up residence above the ceiling of the Florsheim base;

04:35.370 --> 04:39.480
Its identity is such a mystery that Vamp and the others have been hesitant in chasing it out.

04:39.480 --> 04:41.120
What, do you want something?

04:41.120 --> 04:42.940
I've been listening to what you said,

04:42.940 --> 04:43.940
and I'll be frank:

04:43.940 --> 04:47.560
You've got some nerve to be talking like that since you're just a freeloader.

04:48.390 --> 04:50.220
You're one to talk!

04:50.220 --> 04:51.910
You've got it all wrong right down to the basics.

04:51.910 --> 04:56.020
Listen, Kayoko feeds you even though you don't work, right?

04:56.020 --> 04:58.470
How did you know that?

04:58.770 --> 05:00.770
You should at least clean the house everyday.

05:00.770 --> 05:03.670
But every time I clean she always comes to me at the end and tells me I did this and that wrong-

05:03.670 --> 05:04.550
I didn't ask for your opinion on this.

05:07.120 --> 05:08.350
And sit up straight when I talk to you.

05:08.350 --> 05:10.010
Why should I?

05:10.010 --> 05:11.380
I can always leave you know.

05:11.680 --> 05:13.140
What the hell.

05:13.780 --> 05:16.190
Wait a minute, why are you guys sitting up straight too?

05:16.190 --> 05:17.670
We figured it's best.

05:17.670 --> 05:18.430
Look here, you.

05:18.430 --> 05:19.870
What?

05:19.870 --> 05:21.450
You really don't get it at all.

05:21.450 --> 05:26.160
Look, rather than complain about it, you could help out and clean with her.

05:26.560 --> 05:28.810
You're living under the same roof so you should help each other.

05:29.660 --> 05:32.240
You've said that Kayoko's been in a bad mood since the morning,

05:32.240 --> 05:34.570
but that's probably from all the stress building up.

05:34.570 --> 05:35.880
How do you know?

05:35.880 --> 05:38.460
Unagi...

05:38.460 --> 05:41.280
She a solicitor at an insurance firm, right?

05:41.280 --> 05:42.810
Her work's bound to be stressful.

05:42.810 --> 05:44.810
And that's especially why you have to be there for her.

05:45.210 --> 05:47.500
How do you know so much about this?

05:47.500 --> 05:48.100
Never mind that.

05:49.020 --> 05:51.680
Has anything about Kayoko changed recently?

05:51.680 --> 05:53.050
A new haircut, perhaps?

05:54.180 --> 05:54.910
Did you tell him that too?

05:54.910 --> 05:56.150
I haven't said a word about her hair.

05:56.150 --> 05:57.490
That's just based on my intuition.

05:57.490 --> 05:58.060
Intuition?

05:58.860 --> 06:01.870
Girls usually cut their hair after breaking up with someone or after something bad happens;

06:01.870 --> 06:03.220
that's just the way they are.

06:04.020 --> 06:06.130
She did cut her hair, like you said.

06:06.130 --> 06:09.820
So have you mentioned anything to her about it?

06:10.400 --> 06:11.760
Like "that looks good on you" or something.

06:13.050 --> 06:14.650
N-No.

06:14.950 --> 06:16.390
I see.

06:16.390 --> 06:18.880
That's probably why Kayoko's all upset.

06:19.230 --> 06:21.860
She went all the way to the beauty parlor and got dolled up,

06:21.860 --> 06:24.010
but you've failed to even notice.

06:24.210 --> 06:26.880
C-Could that be why?

06:26.880 --> 06:29.460
The biggest sin a man can commit against a woman is disinterest.

06:29.460 --> 06:31.190
You should go back home right now,

06:31.190 --> 06:33.730
and say something about her hair, okay?

06:34.140 --> 06:38.390
Take the rest of the seasoned rice and make rice balls so he can take it back, Vamp.

06:38.730 --> 06:40.760
Kayoko might not have had lunch yet.

06:40.760 --> 06:41.430
O-Okay.

06:41.800 --> 06:44.530
And when you're dealing with a woman her age,

06:44.530 --> 06:45.440
you really should be sensitive about how to-

06:45.440 --> 06:50.370
Now that I think about it, why do you have to take orders from that thing?

06:50.370 --> 06:53.160
Well, it's for Kayoko's sake after all.

06:55.020 --> 06:56.800
All right, I'm gonna head back.

06:58.080 --> 06:59.330
Oh yeah.

06:59.880 --> 07:00.640
Hey Vamp!

07:00.640 --> 07:01.020
Yes?

07:01.020 --> 07:04.610
Stop talking shit and spreading rumors about me when you're back at the base, you punk.

07:05.010 --> 07:05.760
Laters.

07:07.020 --> 07:09.090
He's a complicated man, isn't he?

07:09.090 --> 07:12.280
I hope Kayoko likes the rice balls.

07:13.430 --> 07:14.550
Hey Kayoko!

07:17.160 --> 07:17.970
What's with you?

07:17.970 --> 07:19.960
You haven't had lunch yet right?

07:19.960 --> 07:21.310
You shouldn't eat cup noodles.

07:21.310 --> 07:23.170
I'll make some tea with that water instead.

07:23.920 --> 07:27.150
I had Vamp make some flavored rice balls for you.

07:27.150 --> 07:27.950
Vamp made these?

07:27.950 --> 07:28.930
Yeah.

07:28.930 --> 07:31.060
Go sit down and eat those, okay?

07:33.350 --> 07:34.380
Thanks.

07:35.570 --> 07:36.980
Did you eat already?

07:36.980 --> 07:38.730
Yeah, I ate at Vamp's.

07:42.400 --> 07:43.410
What?

07:44.680 --> 07:47.070
Hey, your...

07:48.530 --> 07:51.560
Your new hair looks really cute.

07:51.910 --> 07:53.990
U-Um,

07:54.390 --> 07:55.760
Mr. Ceiling?

07:55.760 --> 08:01.060
You told Mr. Red earlier that people who live under the same roof should help each other out, right?

08:01.460 --> 08:06.270
We would really appreciate your help on our next operation to kill Mr. Red...

08:13.240 --> 08:16.810
Let's go out for a drink right now!

08:16.810 --> 08:17.620
S-Sure.

08:18.420 --> 08:20.080
You're amazing, Ceiling.

08:20.080 --> 08:21.790
She really did come around.

08:23.280 --> 08:24.490
Is he ignoring us?

08:24.490 --> 08:26.200
Astro Fighter Sunred.

08:26.200 --> 08:28.650
This is the magnificent story of the conflict between good and evil

08:28.650 --> 08:31.140
which takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

08:31.140 --> 08:32.890
Anago...

08:43.460 --> 08:49.000
Ever notice how female celebrities always seem to pull off a decent impersonation of Crayon Shin-chan?

08:49.740 --> 08:51.950
Maybe he's just easy to impersonate.

08:54.140 --> 08:54.880
Maybe.

09:05.920 --> 09:08.840
Master Vamp gave us donuts, you guys!

09:08.840 --> 09:09.950
Here you go, P-chan.

09:09.950 --> 09:11.290
Here, Devilcat.

09:11.290 --> 09:12.960
Oh, I'll pass.

09:14.110 --> 09:16.220
I'm actually restricting my caloric intake.

09:17.230 --> 09:19.900
The doctor told me that I may be diabetic.

09:19.900 --> 09:21.570
Diabetic?

09:21.570 --> 09:22.230
Yeah.

09:22.690 --> 09:23.520
There's something in my urine that's-

09:26.830 --> 09:28.930
And the calculations show...

09:28.930 --> 09:30.570
that this branch isn't doing very well in sales.

09:31.120 --> 09:34.150
Why aren't you guys squeezing every penny out of your customers?

09:34.150 --> 09:35.150
I'm sorry.

09:35.640 --> 09:38.010
Oh, your guest is ready, Mr. Rei.

09:39.590 --> 09:41.510
And tonight I will be servicing...

09:41.510 --> 09:43.890
a 20 year old hostess.

09:45.320 --> 09:48.570
So you've changed your watch to match your hair, I see.

09:49.720 --> 09:52.460
But that watch of yours is a fake.

09:52.460 --> 09:54.950
Really? No way!

09:54.950 --> 09:56.520
I have a good nose, you know.

09:56.520 --> 09:58.670
The customer who gave it to me was a real jerk.

09:58.720 --> 10:02.050
But that's perfect for you right now.

10:03.870 --> 10:04.920
Does that make you mad?

10:05.210 --> 10:08.890
Then why don't you try for "the real deal?"

10:09.770 --> 10:13.420
I'll take away all that stress right here right now.

10:13.960 --> 10:17.230
I'm sure you'll be able to become... the real deal.

10:18.330 --> 10:19.950
Reiji!

10:20.450 --> 10:22.270
You're so soft!

10:22.270 --> 10:24.870
I'm made of 100% cotton, you know.

10:25.270 --> 10:27.710
Here are the three champagne towers you ordered.

10:27.990 --> 10:30.060
Thank you for your patronage!

10:38.880 --> 10:41.490
My new weapon to kill Red is a hammer!

10:41.790 --> 10:42.660
An axe!

10:44.460 --> 10:47.350
I don't think nukes are quite in the same ballpark, P-chan!

10:47.350 --> 10:49.170
We don't have the power to stand up against the whole world yet!

10:56.310 --> 10:58.270
Thank you as always.

10:58.270 --> 10:59.240
Don't mention it.

10:59.240 --> 11:01.660
It always tastes better when you make a lot anyway.

11:02.690 --> 11:05.280
What are you doing, Mr. Red?

11:05.280 --> 11:06.700
Can't you tell?

11:06.700 --> 11:08.330
I'm reorganizing the closet.

11:10.700 --> 11:14.120
What's this "Firebird Form" thing?

11:14.420 --> 11:17.580
You know how heroes tend to power-up somewhere midway through the series

11:17.580 --> 11:19.930
so they can fight even stronger enemies, right?

11:20.230 --> 11:21.540
That's basically what it is.

11:21.540 --> 11:24.380
Firebird Form is my ultimate form.

11:24.780 --> 11:25.580
There we go.

11:26.080 --> 11:30.050
You won't be able to use it right away if you put it in so far back!
